8,Folk Music of the Western Congo | Smithsonian Folkways Recordings,https://folkways.si.edu/folk-music-of-the-western-congo/world/album/smithsonian,"Folk Music of the Western Congo presents music from the Bantu-speaking tribes of Western Congo. Included is a Bambala litigation proceeding, which requires litigants to both speak and sing their case to the village chief. One litigant says, “Let us debate the things, but slowly, slowly….” He then …",Tsaangi,Niger-Congo
9,Niger-Congo languages | African Language Family | Britannica,https://www.britannica.com/topic/Niger-Congo-languages,"July 26, 1999 - Spoken by various ethnic groups, Niger-Congo languages reflect the cultural diversity of the continent. They have shaped musical traditions, with time-line patterns and rhythmic structures integral to many forms of dance music. Oral traditions, including praise poetry, are also closely tied to these languages.",Tsaangi,Niger-Congo
